      "If the new gate will serve a ranch, construction site, or equipment yard, plan enough interior room for vehicles to straighten out after entering. A wide gate alone does not solve a tight turn immediately inside the property. Clearing brush back from the entrance and shaping the approach can improve visibility and make trailer movement easier. Drainage should also be checked because gate entrances often become muddy where traffic repeatedly concentrates. Adding the right grade and preparing the surface before the fence crew finishes can create a more durable entrance and reduce the chance that the new gate area becomes a maintenance problem during the first heavy rain."
